SCHEDULE 5.12(a)

ENVIRONMENTAL MATTERS

 This Schedule sets forth qualifications of the representation and warranty contained in subsection 5.12 of the Agreement relating to environmental matters:

 Batangas - Asian Development Bank (ADB) issued a 1999 Project Performance Audit Report stating that Batangas Power Corp. had not complied with the provisions of DENR [Department of Energy and Natural Resources] Memorandum Circular No. 29 which applies to thermal power plants in non-urban areas.  ADB claims that  Bantagas Power Corp. should have:
  
(m) conducted plume dispersion studies of plant emissions to determine sites for ambient air sampling; and
 
(n) installed automatic continuous ambient air sampling instruments in at least two of the sites verified as appropriate with DENR, and sent the results of this continuous air sampling to DENR each month.

Batangas Power Corp. does not agree with the findings of the ADB report and has been meeting and corresponding with ADB to explain that plume dispersion studies were conducted as early as September of 1993, and that the results of monthly air sampling tests have been sent to the DENR since the project began commercial operations.  Batangas Power Corp. also sought to convince ADB that the DENR no longer requires Batangas Power Corp. to install automatic continuous ambient air sampling instruments because the exemption issued by the President of the Philippines in 1993 applied to environmental regulations during construction and operation.  Discussions with ADB are ongoing.  

   
